<LegalLayout
  title="KYC Policy"
  description="How Trackwise verifies the identity of individuals and businesses on its platform."
  eyebrow="Compliance"
  effective="2026-05-17"
  lastUpdated="2026-05-17"
>
  <p>
    Trackwise applies a Know Your Customer (KYC) and Know Your Business (KYB)
    program built on a risk-based approach and aligned with the BSA / AML
    program described in our <a href="/aml">AML / BSA Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Individual identity verification (KYC)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Government-issued photo identification (passport, national ID, driver's license).</li>
    <li>Selfie with liveness detection, compared against the ID image.</li>
    <li>Address verification through document or authoritative database.</li>
    <li>Tax identifier where required.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Business identity verification (KYB)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Certificate of incorporation / good standing.</li>
    <li>Articles of organization or bylaws.</li>
    <li>Beneficial-owner identification at 25% or greater ownership.</li>
    <li>One control person (e.g., CEO or equivalent).</li>
    <li>Description of business and source of funds.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Vendors</h2>
  <p>
    Identity verification is performed through specialized vendors. Vendors we
    may use include Persona, Sumsub, Veriff, Onfido, Au10tix, and Trulioo. Our
    choice of vendor depends on geography and product. All vendors are subject
    to vendor-risk review and contractual data-protection terms.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Enhanced due diligence (EDD)</h2>
  <p>EDD is applied when the customer or activity presents elevated risk, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Politically exposed persons (PEPs) and their immediate family / close associates.</li>
    <li>Customers based in, or doing business with, high-risk geographies (e.g., FATF-listed jurisdictions).</li>
    <li>High-value or high-velocity transactions inconsistent with the stated profile.</li>
    <li>Adverse media or sanctions hits.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Refresh</h2>
  <p>
    Customer information is refreshed on a risk-based schedule. Higher-risk
    customers are reviewed more frequently.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Prohibited jurisdictions</h2>
  <p>
    Trackwise does not onboard customers located in, organized under the laws
    of, or ordinarily resident in jurisdictions subject to comprehensive U.S.
    sanctions or on the FATF call-for-action list. The list is reviewed and
    updated regularly.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:compliance@trackwise.finance">compliance@trackwise.finance</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
